cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use flexyBayes in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "flexyBayes: Flexible Bayesian Mixed Models with ASReml and brms-Style Syntax"
abstract: >-
  Specify mixed models using familiar ASReml or brms-style formula syntax
  and estimate them via INLA or brms (Stan). The ASReml grammar reaches
  INLA natively, so multi-stratum designs, per-environment residual
  variances, unstructured and factor-analytic genotype-by-environment
  covariance, known-covariance genomic and pedigree models, separable AR1
  spatial fields and univariate P-splines are fitted by approximation
  rather than by sampling. Results are returned in formats compatible with
  the standard R modelling ecosystem. Structures no active engine
  represents raise typed refusals naming the nearest implemented
  alternative.
type: software
